#!/usr/bin/env bash
# refresh-dynamic-cursors — keep the dynamic-cursors plugin checked out at
# the upstream-pinned commit for the running Hyprland version, then rebuild.
#
# Cron-safe contract:
#   • Idempotent — fast no-op when current pin matches running Hyprland AND
#     plugin is loaded
#   • Reads the pin matrix from upstream `origin/main:hyprpm.toml`, NOT the
#     working-tree copy (which is stale at the previous pin's hyprpm.toml)
#   • Stops cleanly with an error if upstream has not yet published a pin for
#     the running Hyprland (raybbian's matrix sometimes lags releases)
#
# Usage: ../run refresh-dynamic-cursors

exec claude -p \
'Refresh the dynamic-cursors plugin at ~/repos/dynamic-cursors so it matches the running Hyprland v0.54.x ABI.

Decision logic — only do work when needed:

(A) Detect state:
  1. Get the running Hyprland git commit hash from `hyprctl version` (the long hex hash, 40 chars).
  2. cd to ~/repos/dynamic-cursors, `git fetch origin`.
  3. Read the pin matrix: `git show origin/main:hyprpm.toml`. Find the line whose FIRST hash matches the running Hyprland commit. The required plugin commit is the SECOND hash on that line.
     • If no matching line exists, STOP and report: "Upstream has no pin for Hyprland <commit>; manual investigation needed". This is a real condition (raybbian sometimes lags) and should not be silently worked around.
  4. Get current HEAD commit hash.
  5. `hyprctl plugin list` — is "dynamic-cursors" currently loaded?

(B) If current HEAD == required pin AND plugin is loaded → report "up to date, no action" and exit. Common case.

(C) Otherwise:
  1. If current HEAD != required pin: `git checkout <pin-hash>`.
  2. Rebuild: `make clean && rm -rf out && make all`. If the build fails, STOP and report compiler errors.
  3. Reload: `hyprctl plugin load /home/komi/repos/dynamic-cursors/out/dynamic-cursors.so`.
  4. Verify: `hyprctl plugin list` shows "dynamic-cursors".

Final summary (one concise paragraph): pin used (with the Hyprland version it maps to), checkout taken or skipped, build outcome, load outcome. If nothing was needed, say so plainly.' \
  --allowed-tools 'Bash(cd *) Bash(git *) Bash(make *) Bash(rm *) Bash(hyprctl *) Bash(grep *) Bash(awk *) Bash(ls *) Bash(stat *) Read Glob Grep'
